,"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["closember","code-quality","hacktoberfest","linter","pep8","static-analysis","static-code-analysis"],"visibility":"public","forks":1204,"open_issues":1060,"watchers":5620,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Many projects (Twisted, Hypothesis, pytest, my own, and probably more) started using [attrs](http://www.attrs.org/) because it makes it much more pleasant to write data classes.\r\n\r\nHowever, pylint doesn't understand attrs' handling of default values:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport attr\r\n\r\n@attr.s\r\nclass Foo:\r\n\r\n    d = attr.ib(attr.Factory(dict))\r\n\r\nf = Foo()\r\nf.d['answer'] = 42\r\n```\r\n\r\noutputs:\r\n\r\n```\r\nE:  9, 0: 'f.d' does not support item assignment (unsupported-assignment-operation)\r\n```\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, I can't find a way to turn this off selectively either, e.g. by adding `Foo` to `ignored-classes`.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/1698/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/1698/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]